TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"attempt":1,"blocked":true,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/26","kind":"diagnosis","posted":true,"proposal":{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\""],"description":"Running the checkpoint command leaves the git worktree completely clean: no modified tracked files and no new untracked files anywhere in the repository.","id":"checkpoint-leaves-worktree-clean"},{"argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh >/dev/null && git diff --exit-code -- results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json results/receipts/weights-worker.json"],"description":"The committed receipt baselines results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json and results/receipts/weights-worker.json are unchanged after the checkpoint command runs.","id":"receipts-not-rewritten"},{"argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh | tee /dev/stderr | grep -q 'both nodes staged'"],"description":"The checkpoint still stages on both nodes and reports success, printing the coordinator and worker summaries and the final 'both nodes staged' line.","id":"validation-still-reports-both-nodes"},{"argv":["bash","-c","! grep -nE 'RECEIPTS=\"?\\$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"],"description":"The script no longer targets the tracked results/receipts directory as its write destination; receipts are collected into a scratch directory outside the worktree.","id":"no-tracked-receipt-writes-in-source"},{"argv":["bash","-c","grep -qE 'status.*pass' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh && grep -q 'shards' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"],"description":"A receipt whose status is not pass, or whose shard count diverges from the committed baseline, causes the checkpoint to exit non-zero rather than silently succeeding.","id":"status-mismatch-is-fatal"}],"dependencies":[],"goal":"Make the cp-weights checkpoint validate the prepared base without writing to tracked files. Change scripts/stage-weights-both.sh so both node receipts are produced into a run-scoped scratch directory outside the repository worktree (for example a mktemp -d, or a directory supplied via an environment variable with a temp-dir default) instead of into results/receipts/ directly. The script must then compare the freshly collected coordinator and worker receipts against the committed baselines results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json and results/receipts/weights-worker.json: fail when either receipt has status other than pass, fail when either shard count differs from the committed baseline, and tolerate drift in the ts field and in data.bytes (report the delta rather than failing on it, or bound it with an explicit documented tolerance). Preserve the existing behaviour of streaming scripts/stage-weights.sh to the worker over ssh and collecting its receipt with scp, keep the human-readable per-host summary lines and the final 'both nodes staged' line, and keep set -euo pipefail. After a successful run, git status --porcelain must be empty: no tracked file under results/receipts/ may be modified and no untracked file may be left inside the worktree. Refreshing the committed baselines must be an explicit separate action, not a side effect of running the checkpoint.","kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/stage-weights-both.sh","scripts/stage-weights.sh"]},"redacted":false,"retry":null,"taskId":"cp-weights","verdict":"blocked"}
